<title>SOUTH KOREA: Samsung in $300 mln Mexico TV glass plant venture.</title>
<headline>Samsung in $300 mln Mexico TV glass plant venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsung Corning Co, a unit of South Korea's Samsung Group, said on Monday it had agreed with Japan's Asahi Glass Co and Corning Inc of the U.S. to build a $300 million colour television glass plant in Mexico.  </p>
<p>Samsung said in a statement the venture would be capable of producing glass for eight million colour TV tubes a year.</p>
<p>It said three firms would jointly manage the plant, but didn't give a breakdown of ownership.</p>
<p>The joint venture would launch a polishing plant in early 1998 and a melting plant in 1999, it added.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
